{"id": "EUVD-2026-102340", "enisaUuid": "26e2f104-5bfb-369c-bf0d-2af7e28480fc", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE from 2.7.1 through 2.9.0 contains a CRLF injection vulnerability in services_unbound_advanced.php that allows authenticated users with DNS Resolver: Advanced privilege to inject Unbound directives. Attackers can embed CR/LF characters in the unvalidated sock_queue_timeout parameter, which is written raw into unbound.conf, to override local records and forwarding for all clients.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T20:02:39", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:L/SA:L", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-unbound-sock-timeout", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/services_unbound_advanced.php#L178", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/unbound.inc#L590", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-2.7.1-through-2.9.0-crlf-injection-via-services-unbound-advanced-php"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3pxq-gxxr-7p9c", "CVE-2026-111228"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.84, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7c6ea428-cbf5-3e03-afbc-209ad78e707d", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "2.7.1 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b6236a76-01fc-354c-b8d6-c5c4e9c2fc27", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}